---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

/* Public twin of src/pages/Terms.tsx in the app repo. Keep the two in step. */
const email = site.contactEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Amor Budget"
  description="The terms you agree to when you create an Amor Budget account."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="August 16, 2026"
>
  <p>Create an account and use Amor Budget, and you agree to what follows.</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Amor Budget tracks your income and spending against a Needs, Wants and Savings split you set yourself. It
    organises what you type in. It does not reach your bank, move your money, or advise you on what to do with it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    Keep your sign-in details to yourself, and enter figures you believe are right. The app works from what you
    give it. You need to be old enough to enter a binding agreement where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Track your own household budget. Do not go after another user's data, do not disrupt the service for anyone
    else, and do not use the app to break the law.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We provide Amor Budget as it is. We work to keep it accurate and running, and we still cannot promise it will
    never break or go offline. It stands in for no accountant and no financial adviser.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending your account</h2>
  <p>
    Delete your account whenever you like, from Profile. Your data goes with it, at once and for good. We may
    suspend or close an account that breaks these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms will change as the app does. When something material changes, it appears here and the date at the
    top of this page moves.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this? Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
